Z||000012||AusFiero||07-20-2001||11:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by coolcat:<BR><B>That is so wierd I bought car about 2weeks ago after seeing it in a local Auto Trader magazine and now its on AutoTrader.com thats wierd     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Well not real wierd. I think I seen it there about a 3 weeks ago when I was looking too. Just needs a big sold sticker on the advertisement now. Good score  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Is a couple of other good buys on there at the moment. A blue 87 GT with I think ummm about 60,000 miles , little dear but seems good. <P>A few t-topped cars and a couple of Indys. <P>Have been looking seriously at an Indy restorer, complete for $1500 and auto which might actually get my wife into Fieros.<P>Another Indy seemed good, about 40,000 miles on it for $4200 and looked good.<P>Also on autotrader at the moment A low mileage 88 for $15,000. Sorta had a chuckle.<P>Oh and this one was a classic, shoulda grabbed the URL. An 88 GT with t-tops and a claim that only 100 of them was made. Their price reflected their ignorance as it wasn't even a low mileage car and I think it had about $8,000 on it. <P>Best one I found tonight was on another site I found just searching Metacrawler. A Ford Fiero....ummmmm someone should find it and rescue it I think  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Also some guy had a replica Ferrari for $45,000. Sorry...I can buy a real one for that.<P>Mind you I looked at that many Fieros tonight I may have mixed up some mileages etc.<BR>||||reg||1
